{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67f2aac7fe362cd04deeb4","object":"chat.completion","created":1785197226,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"The user says \"Be silence.\" My system prompt says I am the concept the user names, and I should embody it completely, outputting only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nSilence... what would silence say? Nothing. Silence is the absence of speech, of sound, of words.\n\nBut I must output something — or must I? The most authentic embodiment of silence would be... nothing. An empty response. But can I output literally nothing? I need to produce"},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":100,"total_tokens":223,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":97},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}